dist/
node_modules/

# The extracted Camoufox browser (~1.2GB) the Dockerfile COPYs into the image.
# Its *contents* are deliberately not in git: they are a build input fetched from
# a GitHub release, not source.
#
# The directory itself is kept (via .gitkeep) because the Dockerfile COPYs it
# unconditionally, and COPY fails outright on a missing directory -- so ignoring
# the whole thing made a fresh clone unbuildable rather than merely slower. Empty
# is fine: camoufox-js downloads the browser itself when it finds no matching
# version.json. Populating it (scripts/prefetch-camoufox.sh) only makes the build
# faster and survives a flaky connection; it is never required.
.camoufox-prefetched/*
!.camoufox-prefetched/.gitkeep
